  "notes": "Per the 2026-2027 Texas A&M University undergraduate catalog: Nursing — Accelerated BSN Track (BSN). Prerequisites are not listed in the catalog's plan of study grid; consult course descriptions.\nCatalog footnotes:\n[grid1 fn1] Core Curriculum courses are listed on the University Core Curriculum page. STAT 201 is recommended to fulfill 3 hours of Mathematics, but is not required.\n[grid1 fn2] Indicates Nursing Science course.\n[grid1 fn3] These courses may be taken at a community college, but must be completed by the first day at the School of Nursing. Students may elect to place these courses anywhere in their schedule, though it is encouraged that these be completed over the summer.\n[grid1 fn4] Texas common courses BIOL 2401 and 2402 taken at any Texas accredited public institution will meet the requirement for BIOL 319 and BIOL 320 .",
